# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Dwarf Cannon" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Captain Lawgof
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Captain Lawgof	Guthix be praised, the cavalry has arrived! Hero, how would you like to be made an honorary member of the Black Guard?
1	line	Player	The Black Guard? What's that?
1	line	Captain Lawgof	Hawhaw! 'What's that' [he/she] asks, what a sense of humour! The Black Guard is the finest regiment in the dwarven army. Only the best of the best are allowed to join it and then they receive months of rigorous training.
1	line	Captain Lawgof	However, we are currently in need of a hero, so for a limited time only I'm offering you, a human, a chance to join this prestigious regiment. What do you say?
1	select	Start the Dwarf Cannon quest?
1	option	Yes.
2	line	Player	Sure, I'd be honoured to join.
2	line	Captain Lawgof	That's the spirit! Now trooper, we have no time to waste - the goblins are attacking from the forests to the South. There are so many of them, they are overwhelming my men and breaking through our
2	line	Captain Lawgof	perimeter defences; could you please try to fix the stockade by replacing the broken rails with these new ones?
2	line	Player	Sure, sounds easy enough...
2	box	The Dwarf Captain gives you six railings.
2	cond	If the player does not have a hammer:
3	line	Captain Lawgof	You'll need this hammer too.
3	action	
2	line	Captain Lawgof	Report back to me once you've fixed the railings.
2	line	Player	Yes Sir, Captain!
2	action	end
1	option	No.
2	line	Player	I'm sorry, I'm too busy mining.
2	line	Captain Lawgof	Well best make the most of it while you can, if the goblins over-run us they'll descend on the mines like a plague of locusts!
2	action	end
0	section	Inspecting the broken multicannon
1	box	The Black Guard sent Lawgof this cannon to help defend the mines against the goblins.
1	action	end
