1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Captain Lawgof	Have you been to the watch tower yet?
1	line	Player	Yes, I went up but there was no one there.
1	line	Captain Lawgof	That's strange, Gilob would never leave his post... His son was also with him, something doesn't smell right. Can you return and look for clues?
1	line	Player	Of course, I'll do what I can.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Captain Lawgof after getting the remains
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Captain Lawgof	Have you been to the watch tower yet?
1	line	Player	I have some terrible news for you Captain, the goblins over ran the tower, your guards fought well but were overwhelmed.
1	box	You give the Dwarf Captain his subordinate's remains...
1	line	Captain Lawgof	I can't believe it, Gilob was the finest lieutenant I had! We'll give him a fitting funeral, but what of his command? His son, Lollk, was with him. Did you find his body too?
1	line	Player	No, there was only one body there, I searched pretty well.
1	line	Captain Lawgof	The goblins must have taken him. Please traveler, seek out the goblins' hideout and return the lad to us. They always attack from the South-east, so they must be based down there.
1	line	Player	Okay, I'll see if I can find their hideout.
1	action	end
0	section	The dwarf child
0	section	Searching the crate containing Lollk before returning the remains
0	section	Searching the crate containing Lollk
1	line	Lollk	Thank the heavens, you saved me! I thought I'd be goblin lunch for sure!
1	line	Player	Are you okay?
1	line	Lollk	I think so, I'd better run off home.
1	line	Player	That's right, you get going, I'll catch up.
1	line	Lollk	Thanks again, brave adventurer.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Captain Lawgof after finding Lollk
1	line	Player	Hello, has Lollk returned yet?
1	line	Captain Lawgof	He has, and I thank you from the bottom of my heart - without you he'd be a goblin barbecue!
1	line	Player	Always a pleasure to help.
1	line	Captain Lawgof	In that case could I ask one more favour of you...
1	line	Captain Lawgof	When the goblins attacked us some of them managed to slip past my guards and sabotage our cannon. I don't have anybody who understands how it works, could you have a look at it and see if you could get it working for
1	line	Captain Lawgof	us, please?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Okay, I'll see what I can do.
2	line	Player	Okay, I'll see what I can do.
2	line	Captain Lawgof	Thank you, take this toolkit, you'll need it...
2	cond	If the player has no inventory space:
3	line	Captain Lawgof	You don't have room to take this, report back to me when you do.
3	action	end
2	line	Captain Lawgof	Report back to me if you manage to fix it.
2	action	end
1	option	Sorry, I've done enough for today.
2	line	Player	Sorry, I've done enough for today.
2	line	Captain Lawgof	Fair enough, didn't think you'd be able to help anyway, not much chance for a human to be able to fix it when the best dwarven engineers have failed.
2	action	end
